.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt IWM 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm iwm
.Nd Intel(R) Dual Band Wireless-AC 8260 and 8265 Driver
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver is a GLDv3-based
.Em 802.11b/g/n
wireless NIC driver for the Intel Dual Band Wireless-AC 8260 and 8265
(8000 series) adapters.
It supports station mode in infrastructure networks, open and WPA2-PSK
(CCMP) networks, HT20 operation on the 2.4 GHz band with a single
spatial stream, and transmit A-MPDU aggregation.
.Pp
The 5 GHz band, 40 MHz channels, multiple spatial streams, 802.11ac,
power save, and suspend and resume are not currently supported.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The following properties may be set in
.Pa /kernel/drv/iwm.conf :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy iwm-public-scan
When set to 0 the driver attaches passively and does not register a
wireless link.
The default is 1.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -compact -width Pa
.It Pa /dev/iwm*
Special character device.
.It Pa /kernel/drv/amd64/iwm
64-bit ELF kernel module (x86).
.It Pa /kernel/firmware/iwm/iwm-8000C-36
Firmware for the 8260.
.It Pa /kernel/firmware/iwm/iwm-8265-36
Firmware for the 8265.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dladm 8 ,
.Xr wificonfig 8
